Z||000016||DKOV||12-07-2001||01:57 AM||||Spyder:<P>I just took a look through your other pics and I really like the job you did with the Xplode subwoofers!  Thy tucked nicely back there.  Did you build boxes or just cut some holes?<P>Also, what kind of Steering wheel is that?<P>Last comment is to the seats... They look GREAT!  Triple stitched!!!  Are those custom done locally or are those a set of Mr. Mikes seats?<P>All in all, your car looks great!!!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000017||rogergarrison||12-07-2001||06:13 AM||||Ive seen some of the spacers. There priced almost as high as extended A arms. If you go that route, dont do any 'sporty' driving. Ive seen Ferrari tailite sets for under $200 a set on EBay. BTW, only the US versions have the backup lite in rear lens. Euro ones either dont have them at all, or there under the bumpers like fog lites. Dont quote me on that for newer models, I dont have euro sales catalogs to see for later stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000018||artherd||12-07-2001||01:22 PM||||No offence, infact I REALLY like the car you're building, but subwoffers, tripple stitched seats, and NO held suspension?<P>PS: dosen't look like 2" is enough in the rear there either.<P>Good luck with the car, I know what it feels like to go 'all out' (ordering my 3-plate clutch today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000019||Spyder||12-07-2001||09:03 PM||||Rogergarrison: the 355 has the clear center in all of the taillights, I know where you were coming from, this car started as a 328.  I took the 328 body off and sold it to buy the 355 body.  Oh, and something neat on the euro version, the outside taillights have yellow bulbs inside the clear for turn signals.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/328c.JPG">  <BR>DKOV: I built some custom boxes and cut the rear firewall fiberglassed it in, in honor of “fierosound”.<BR>The steering wheel is a LeCarra, it was inexpensive.<BR>The seats are Corbellu(spelling?) they are a little wide, and I had to weld some brackets to make them work. I picked them up from summit.<BR>Artherd: No offence taken, everyone does things different, that what I like about modifying things, there are no rules…<BR>Artherd, BTW love your headlights, (sounds kind of funny.)<BR>On my suspension, I don’t have the held suspension because I had spent so much on the one that I have.  I sent my adjustable Koni struts back to Koni and had them take two inches off the length of the body of the strut and had them shorten the rod. So this car is very low with the lowering springs.  That one pic wasn't a good example, an optical illusion:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1355mm3.JPG">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1355mm4.JPG"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000020||mshill||12-16-2001||03:37 PM||||Here's my dillemma...<P>I really like the ROH ZS wheels like Spyder has on his 355.  They are about as close to the real F50 wheels I can find.  The problem is that they don't come in a 5x100 bolt pattern.  With the Held setup I would still have the crappy 5x100 bolt pattern and still<BR>need some kind of adapter to get to the ROH ZS wheels.<P>I have found other wheels that I would put on the F50, but nobody seems to make a 17 inch rim wider than 8 inches for the 5x100 bolt pattern unless it is a 3 pc custom like the compomotive ZS or Ronal R67. <P>The compomotive wheels are styled more for the 308, 328 models, not the later models F355 or F50.  The TS solution for my F50 would be $2200 and a set of wheel bearings every year.<P>I am leaning towards getting the Ronal R67 17x8 (-35mm) for the fronts and 17x9 or 17x10 (-19mm) rears and run 2 inch spacers like theogre recommends and keeping the 5x100 bolt pattern for a future Held Wide Sport setup.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||artherd||12-16-2001||09:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spyder:<BR><B><BR>Artherd: No offence taken, everyone does things different, that what I like about modifying things, there are no rules…<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep!  That's the great part about our cars, you can do almost *anything* with them!  (and you can always swap in the Held components later if you're so inclined, maybe even with their 13" brakes, mmmm!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Maaaan that car is looking good!  How did you do the paint? It looks absolutely beautiful!<P>The 355 is probally one of, if not THE, most beautiful car in the world for me, so I *understand* why you are making one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>PS: If you like, email me about the HID lights, they're actually really easy to do, just cost about $600 in parts :S)  Boy I love 'em though, light up the road like nobody's buisness! (and just make everything look really pretty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
